{"id": "EUVD-2026-107371", "enisaUuid": "ae062874-6bf9-35cd-bbf2-1df9b034f712", "description": "Multiple Cisco products are affected by a vulnerability in the Snort 3 NetFlow Detection Engine that could allow an unauthenticated, remote attacker to cause the Snort 3 Detection Engine to restart, resulting in an interruption of packet inspection.\r\n\r\nThis vulnerability is due to incomplete error checking when Snort 3 parses UDP Netflow Protocol packets. An attacker could exploit this vulnerability by sending a single crafted Netflow packet through an established connection to be parsed by Snort 3. A successful exploit could allow the attacker to cause the Snort 3 Detection Engine to restart unexpectedly, resulting in a DoS condition.", "datePublished": "2026-10-21T16:12:20", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-22T19:10:53", "baseScore": 5.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:C/C:N/I:N/A:L", "references": ["https://sec.cloudapps.cisco.com/security/center/content/CiscoSecurityAdvisory/cisco-sa-snort3-misc-dos-6mB22qAK"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-20019", "GHSA-pqhw-xr48-3362"], "assigner": "cisco", "epss": 0.42, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "03607802-df25-374e-b458-008283f75b5a", "product": {"name": "Cisco Open Source Snort3", "vendor": {"name": "Cisco"}}, "product_version": "3.9.5.0"}, {"id": "042ff23c-67ea-392d-9ed1-7fbd67694abb", "product": {"name": "Cisco UTD SNORT IPS Engine Software", "vendor": {"name": "Cisco"}}, "product_version": "17.12.5"}, {"id": "0502c844-c0f7-3cb2-a7ec-2f75fee188ac", "product": {"name": "Cisco Open Source Snort3", "vendor": {"name": "Cisco"}}, "product_version": "3.1.82.0"}, {"id": "06abf7ae-eee8-38b1-ac07-58730a413220", "product": {"name": "Cisco Secure Firewall Threat Defense (FTD) Software", "vendor": {"name": "Cisco"}}, "product_version": "7.0.2.1"}, {"id": "0a79fe9c-7d61-39a1-9342-9a8121b5873c", "product": {"name": "Cisco Open Source Snort3", "vendor": {"name": "Cisco"}}, "product_version": "3.7.2.0"}, {"id":